Ok, just did some wiztesting, the results were... unexpected.

To prepare, I ^G created red molds to fill an entire level while standing on
the downstairs.  (I didn't dig it out, but I think that's an acceptable
difference)  I then levelported up one level, and walked down the stairs.
right off the bat, I found a surprise.  I wasn't warped, the red mold that was
sitting on the upstairs was shoved, and now the downstairs was covered
instead.  So no shortcut, there.

Next, I levelported down one, and ^Wished for the Amulet of Yendor.
^Identified it to be the real thing (yes, I know, but good habits die hard)
and ^G created the Wizard of Yendor, then waited for him to steal the Amulet.
He double troubled, then one of them stole the amulet. Once he had it, I poked
him with a sharp MagicBane until he fled upstairs.  To make sure I also scared
his double until *he* went up as well.  I followed them, and sure enough, no
Wizard, no Amulet.  So, yeah.  That's bad.  I then level ported up
one level, just to make sure he wasn't there.  He wasn't.  I walked down the
stairs, and got 'problem placing monster on map, perhaps you'd better #quit',
and lo, there was a purple @ on the downstairs across the level, where a red
mold had been before.  I made some space, and he ported over to me where I
killed him, but he was the double without the Amulet.

In conclusion: not a shortcut.  Doesn't warp.  Does lose monsters in transit,
and sometimes they come back and sometimes they don't.

Ok, good to know.  Now, back to my regularly scheduled pudding farming.

